From: jay3332 <me@jay3332.tech>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 12:36:11 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] paragraph-layout: set an empty line when a break lies
 inside the discardables after a break
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

`line_start` skips every discardable after a break, so a forced break
followed only by penalties and glue (`\\` at the end of a paragraph:
`ParagraphBuilder::finish` appends `\penalty10000 \parfillskip
\penalty-10000`; or two consecutive `\\`) put the next line's start past the
next legal break and `set_line` panicked with
`slice index starts at N but ends at N-1`. Total-fit also silently
mis-measured such candidate lines (negative width/stretch, treated as
infeasible) whenever it did not panic.

TeX sets an empty line here (§837 `break_width` drops the discardables'
widths, §879 prunes them, the penalty is still a legal break): the
"Underfull \hbox (badness 10000)" empty line pdflatex prints for a trailing
`\\`. `measure` and `set_line` now clamp `start` to `brk` (an empty line is
`items == brk..brk`), and first-fit resumes at a forced penalty inside the
discarded run instead of jumping over it, so it sets the same empty line as
total-fit.

Golden and oracle outputs are byte-identical; see the handoff README for
the before/after dump comparison.

